  "preamble": "Devoicing of the alveolar implosive to [t], here in two steps. Proto-Austroasiatic *ɗ appears as Old Khmer d (ទិក៑ dik 'water', ទុំ duṃ 'ripe'), and Old Khmer voiced stops later lost their voicing, with the contrast surviving as vowel register: Modern Khmer ទឹក /tɨk/, ទុំ /tum/, ទាក់ /tĕəʔ/. Chong (Pearic) ta̤k 'trap' has the same outcome with breathy voice. Modern Khmer ɗ (ដ) is secondary, from earlier *t (ដៃ 'hand' < Proto-Mon-Khmer *t₁iiʔ).",
